A||||9||chris6878||Small Block 400 V8||||
Z||000000||chris6878||09-05-99||05:41 PM||||Hey...<br>Does anyone know if it is possible to put a 400 small block V8 in a fiero... Does this motor bolt up differently than the 350 and is it bigger in size and length...???? <p>Thanks in advance...<br>Chris
Z||000001||Cooter||09-05-99||07:31 PM||||The 400 small block shares the same external diminsions as the 350, or the 265 or 283. . . With the 400's tendency to overheat, it might not be the best choice. Be sure to use the 400 heads and head gaskets, or have other small block heads drilled for the 400's steam holes.
Z||000002||88 Fiero||09-05-99||07:56 PM||||you probably want to contact Gary Zumalt...he  build a fiero with a 400 CID block for the Pontiac Division strictly for show and this car also is drivable...he sells the V8 kit which is very outstanding...looks like factory after hook up your 350 TPI engine on the Fiero and considered as one of the best V8 Kit around....
Z||000003||chris6878||09-06-99||01:43 PM||||88fiero...<p>How could i contanct this "Gary Zumalt" you mentioned that offered the V8 kit....<br>Is this a better kit than V8 archies...???<br>Is there an email address or a web page i could contact him by...   <p>thanks alot....<p>chris
Z||000004||pherder||09-06-99||05:19 PM||||Last I heard, Gary Zumult is out of the business.<p>There are many copy cat versions of his setup being sold (Shelby http://www.shelbycustom.com/index.html and Gary's Custom Exotics http://www.gscustom.com/ are two that I have seen their web site ads) but they all require cutting the Fiero's frame to fit the transaxle.<p>V8Archie's kit does require cutting the strut tower for water pump clearance but the sheet metal there isn't structural like the frame.<p>
Z||000005||batboy||09-11-1999||10:26 AM||||As mentioned by some of the other informed members, the 400 small bock engine will fit anywhere a 350 will go. The 400 is also externally balanced and uses a different flywheel and balancer than the rest of the internally balanced small blocks (350, 327, 283, etc.). The 400 engine must use 400 heads with the steam holes or like Cooter said, modify the standard heads with steam holes. Some 400 engines seem to run a little hot, which is not great because the Fiero engine compartment is a little too warm anyway.<P>A better way to get more cubic inches is to take a 4 bolt main 350 block and buy one of those 383 stroker kits that comes with a machined down 400 crank, special pistons and rods. This really adds a lot of low end torque and power.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||09-11-1999||02:22 PM||||Unless you have a blower,or over 14:1 compression,you really don't need the truck(4 bolt main)block,but,from what I've found,rods,crankcase ventilation,and valvetrain are where you want to take the caution.<BR>A tunnel ram will help alot too for big HP.<BR>A 383 with some good headwork,and intake will be very,very strong,probably will have to take off from a start in second gear!<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 09-11-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||88 Fiero||09-11-1999||02:59 PM||||hmmmm I don't think Gary is out of business...I've seen an article a few months ago that he had a complete exact tube frame for a Lamborghini Diablo in a show...I will ask my freind Keith and find out if he still in business or not...also I don't know if anyone knows...Gary invented a collapsible engine cradle.. the benefit of this is that when it's time to replace the clutch you don't have to drop the engine...you could lift the whole car and take out half of the engine cradle to get access to clutch...really neat cradle..and I've seen this cradle...this would be a benefit for a fiero...||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||09-11-1999||03:25 PM||||LowCG, you're right, the 2 bolt main 350 small blocks are very tough in all but racing situations. It's just that I have several 4 bolt main 350 engine blocks laying around, so I tend to get rid of the 2 bolt main ones.||||reg||1
Z||000009||88 Fiero||09-11-1999||07:19 PM||||okay...ran into Gary Zumalt's phone no. it's 816-923-4376...good luck!!!||||reg||1
